    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">GICR_PIDR2</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Redistributor Peripheral Identification Register 2</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>Provides information to identify an external Redistributor component.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_GICR_PIDR is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to GICR_PIDR2 are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
        <p>A copy of this register is provided for each Redistributor.</p>
      <h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>GICR_PIDR2 is a 32-bit register.</p>
      <h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="24"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_8">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="4"><a href="#fieldset_0-7_4">ArchRev</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-3_3">JEDEC</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="3"><a href="#fieldset_0-2_0">DES_1</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_8">Bits [31:8]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-7_4">ArchRev, bits [7:4]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Revision field for the GIC architecture. The value of this field depends on the GIC architecture version that applies to the Redistributor.</p>
    <p> The value of this field is an <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span> choice of:</p><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>ArchRev</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0001</td><td>
          <p>GICv1</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0010</td><td>
          <p>GICv2</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0011</td><td>
          <p>GICv3</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0100</td><td>
          <p>GICv4</p>
        </td></tr></table><p>Access to this field is <span class="access_level">RO</span>.</p></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-3_3">JEDEC, bit [3]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>JEDEC-assigned JEP106 implementer code is used.</p>
    
      <p>Reads as <span class="binarynumber">0b1</span>.</p>
    <p>Access to this field is <span class="access_level">RO</span>.</p></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-2_0">DES_1, bits [2:0]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Designer, JEP106 identification code, bits [6:4].</p>
<p>The JEP106 identification and continuation codes are stored as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="ext-gicr_pidr1.html">GICR_PIDR1</a>.DES_0: JEP106 identification code bits[3:0].
</li><li><a href="ext-gicr_pidr2.html">GICR_PIDR2</a>.DES_1: JEP106 identification code bits[6:4].
</li><li><a href="ext-gicr_pidr4.html">GICR_PIDR4</a>.DES_2: JEP106 continuation code.
</li></ul>
<p>These codes indicate the designer of the component and not the implementer, except where the two are the same. To obtain a number, or to see the assignment of these codes, contact JEDEC http://www.jedec.org.</p>
<p>A JEP106 identification and continuation code takes the following form:</p>
<ul>
<li>A sequence of zero or more numbers, all having the value <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span>.
</li><li>A following 8-bit number, that is not <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span>, and where bit[7] is an odd parity bit.
</li></ul>
<p>The parity bit in the JEP106 identification code is not included.</p>
<div class="note"><p>For example, Arm Limited is assigned the code <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span> <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span> <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span> <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span> <span class="hexnumber">0x3B</span>.</p><ul><li>The continuation code is the number of times <span class="hexnumber">0x7F</span> appears before the final number. For example, a component designed by Arm Limited has the code <span class="hexnumber">0x4</span>.</li><li>The identification code is bits[6:0] of the final number. For example, a component designed by Arm Limited has the code <span class="hexnumber">0x3B</span>.</li></ul></div>
      <p>This field has an <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span> value.</p>
    <p>Access to this field is <span class="access_level">RO</span>.</p></div><h2>Accessing GICR_PIDR2</h2><h4>GICR_PIDR2 can be accessed through the memory-mapped interfaces:</h4><table class="info"><tr><th>Component</th><th>Frame</th><th>Offset</th><th>Instance</th></tr><tr><td>GIC Redistributor</td><td>RD_base</td><td><span class="hexnumber">0xFFE8</span></td><td>GICR_PIDR2</td></tr></table><p>Accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RO</span>.</p><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
